WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.752
Hello, my name is Anya, 

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:05.213
and tonight I will be reading

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:07.173
The Witcher: Blood of Elves. 

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.219
In this part of the story, 

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:14.431
Dandelion, who you know
 as Jaskier, is getting tortured.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.474
Let's begin. 

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:23.606
"Well?" Rience
 made a sign to the reeking man.

00:00:23.606 --> 00:00:25.150
"Where is the witcher hiding? 

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.610
“What is the place called?" 

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:30.030
The poet remained silent. 

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:35.160
The rope tightened, twisting his hands
 painfully and his feet left the ground.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.996
Dandelion let out a howl,
brief and broken

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:41.875
because Rience’s wizardly ring
immediately gagged him.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:46.588
"Higher, higher."
 Rience rested his hands on his hips.

00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:48.173
"You know, Dandelion, 

00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:51.551
I could use magic to sound out
your mind, but it’s exhausting.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:55.263
Besides, I like seeing people’s eyes
pop out of their sockets from pain.

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:58.058
And you’re going to tell me anyway."

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.185
Dandelion knew he would.

00:01:00.185 --> 00:01:02.645
The rope secured to
his ankles grew taut, 

00:01:02.645 --> 00:01:07.025
the bucket of lime
 scraped along the ground.

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:10.904
"Sir," said the first ruffian suddenly,
 covering the lantern with his cloak

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.323
and peering through the
gap in the pigsty door,

00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:14.824
"Someone’s coming.

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:16.659
A lass, I think." 

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:19.412
"You know what to do,"
 Rience hissed.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.164
"Put the lantern out."

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:23.083
The reeking man released the rope

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.293
and Dandelion tumbled
inertly to the ground,

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:28.129
falling in such a way that he could see
the man with the lantern standing

00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:31.883
at the door and the reeking man,
a long knife in his hand,

00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:33.927
lying in wait on the other side.

00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:38.598
Light broke in from the bawdy-house
 through gaps in the planks,

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.059
and the poet heard
the singing and hubbub.

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:44.938
The door to the pigsty creaked open
 revealing a short figure

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:48.358
wrapped in a cloak and
wearing a round, tightly fitting cap.

00:01:48.858 --> 00:01:52.487
After a moment’s hesitation,
 the woman crossed the threshold.

00:01:53.696 --> 00:01:57.867
The reeking man threw himself at her,
 slashing forcefully with his knife,

00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:01.162
and tumbled to his knees
 as the knife met with no resistance,

00:02:01.162 --> 00:02:04.457
passing through the figure’s throat
 as though through a cloud of smoke.

00:02:04.874 --> 00:02:07.752
Because the figure really
 was a cloud of smoke

00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:10.338
one which was already
starting to disperse.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.674
But before it completely vanished 

00:02:12.674 --> 00:02:14.342
another figure burst into the pigsty,

00:02:14.342 --> 00:02:16.678
 indistinct, dark
and nimble as a weasel.

00:02:17.345 --> 00:02:19.514
Dandelion saw it
throw a cloak at the lantern man, 

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:21.099
 jump over the reeking one,

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.809
saw something glisten in its hand,

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.728
and heard the reeking
 man wheeze and choke savagely.

00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:28.523
The lantern man disentangled himself
from the cloak,

00:02:28.523 --> 00:02:30.358
 jumped, took a swing with his knife.

00:02:30.358 --> 00:02:33.611
A fiery lightning bolt shot from
the dark figure with a hiss,

00:02:33.611 --> 00:02:36.281
slapped over the tough’s
face and chest with a crack

00:02:36.281 --> 00:02:38.908
 and spread over him like flaming oil.

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:40.869
The ruffian screamed piercingly 

00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:43.663
and the grim reek of burning meat
 filled the pigsty.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.666
Then Rience attacked. 

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.918
The spell he cast
illuminated the darkness

00:02:48.918 --> 00:02:50.920
 with a bluish flame
in which Dandelion

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.464
saw a slender woman
wearing man’s clothes

00:02:53.464 --> 00:02:56.509
 gesticulating strangely
with both hands.

00:02:57.468 --> 00:02:59.637
He only glimpsed her for a second

00:02:59.637 --> 00:03:03.808
before the blue glow disappeared
 with a bang and a blinding flash.

00:03:03.808 --> 00:03:06.853
Rience fell back with a roar of fury
 and collapsed

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:10.440
onto the wooden pigsty walls,
 breaking them with a crash.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.443
The woman dressed in 
man’s clothing leapt after him,

00:03:13.443 --> 00:03:14.944
 a stiletto flashing in her hand.

00:03:15.486 --> 00:03:19.240
The pigsty filled with brightness again
 - this time golden -

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.744
beaming from a bright oval
 which suddenly appeared in the air.

00:03:22.744 --> 00:03:25.788
Dandelion saw Rience
 spring up from the dusty floor,

00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:28.833
leap into the oval
 and immediately disappear.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:32.420
The oval dimmed, but
before it went out entirely, the woman

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.547
ran up to it shouting
incomprehensively,

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.424
stretching out her hand.

00:03:36.424 --> 00:03:39.677
Something crackled and rustled
and the dying oval boiled over,

00:03:39.677 --> 00:03:42.096
 roaring with flames for a moment.

00:03:42.764 --> 00:03:45.642
A muffled sound
as if coming from a great distance

00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:49.270
reached Dandelion’s ears, a sound
 very much like a scream of pain.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.441
The oval went out completely and
darkness engulfed the pigsty again.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.946
The poet felt the power which
gagged him disappear.

00:03:58.446 --> 00:04:00.573
“Help!” he howled. 

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.242
“Help!” 

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:06.037
“Stop yelling, Dandelion,” 
said the woman, kneeling next to him

00:04:06.037 --> 00:04:09.207
and slicing through the knots
with Rience’s stiletto.

00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:11.251
“Yennefer is that you?”

00:04:12.543 --> 00:04:15.088
“Surely you’re not going to
 say you don’t remember how I look.

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:17.590
And I’m sure my voice is not
unfamiliar to your musical ear.”

00:04:18.049 --> 00:04:19.342
“Can you get up?” 

00:04:19.342 --> 00:04:21.386
“They didn’t break
 any bones, did they?”

00:04:21.386 --> 00:04:23.346
Dandelion stood with difficulty, 

00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:26.474
groaned and stretched
his aching shoulders.

00:04:26.474 --> 00:04:27.850
“What’s with them?”

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:30.895
He indicated
 the bodies lying on the ground.

00:04:30.895 --> 00:04:31.938
“We’ll check.”

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:34.107
The enchantress
snicked the stiletto shut.

00:04:35.483 --> 00:04:37.110
“One of them should still be alive.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.237
I’ve a few questions for him.”

00:04:39.237 --> 00:04:42.282
 “This one,” the troubadour stood
over the reeking man, 

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:44.033
“probably still lives.”

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.869
“I doubt it,”
said Yennefer indifferently.

00:04:46.869 --> 00:04:49.372
“I severed his windpipe
 and carotid artery.

00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:51.666
There might still be
 a little murmur in him

00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:52.875
but not for long.” 

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.169
Dandelion shuddered.

00:04:55.878 --> 00:04:58.548
“You slashed his throat?”

00:04:58.548 --> 00:05:00.550
“If, out of inborn caution,

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:04.220
I hadn’t sent an illusion in first,
 I would be the one lying there now.”

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:06.055
“Let’s look at the other one…

00:05:06.055 --> 00:05:09.017
“Bloody hell... such a sturdy fellow
 and he still couldn’t take it.

00:05:09.017 --> 00:05:10.727
Pity, pity—” 

00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:11.811
“He’s dead, too?”

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:13.980
“He coudn’t take the shock

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:17.942
Hmm… I fried him a little
too hard… See,

00:05:17.942 --> 00:05:19.527
even his teeth are charred.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.738
 What’s the matter
with you, Dandelion?

00:05:21.738 --> 00:05:23.323
Are you going to be sick?”

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:24.615
“I am,”

00:05:24.615 --> 00:05:26.451
the poet replied indistinctly, 

00:05:26.451 --> 00:05:29.495
bending over and leaning his
 forehead on the pigsty wall.

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:32.040
Poor Jaskier. 

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:36.127
I think we will leave it there,
 but thank you for joining me

00:05:36.127 --> 00:05:38.087
and I bid you all a good night.

